  "confirmed_source_conclusions": [
    {
      "area": "Root-selection cause and no-global-SDK-write design",
      "references": [
        "installed bin/avdmanager:9-31,67,164-180",
        "avdmanager20-exact-bytecode-01.txt:141-220",
        "repo-local-loader-cli20-bytecode-01.txt:33-70,88-178,355-437,525-652"
      ],
      "conclusion": "Wrapper bakes its Homebrew APP_HOME into com.android.sdkmanager.toolsdir; exact CLI20 init derives SDK from its grandparent, not ANDROID_HOME alone. The real repository scanner writes .knownPackages even with valid packages and can truncate/replace package.xml on fallback. A private owned SDK containing independent selected-image clones prevents those legitimate scanner writes from affecting the installed SDK."
    },
    {
      "area": "Installed class provenance counter-check",
      "references": [
        "installed-tool-bytecode-receipt-01.json",
        "additional-installed-bytecode-receipt-01.json"
      ],
      "conclusion": "tools.sdklib.jar used for AvdManager disassembly is not directly in the actual avdmanager manifest. Independently reopened actual manifest and all referenced JARs: AvdManager.class in sdklib.core.jar and AvdManagerCli.class in libavdmanager_lib.jar are byte-identical to the disassembled tools.sdklib.jar copies; repository loader duplicates are also byte-identical. Thus this apparent version/reachability mismatch is rejected, not ignored."
    },
    {
      "area": "Clone ABI, independence and bounded resources",
      "references": [
        "owned_sdk_image.py:19-168",
        "installed-clonefile.h:32-49",
        "installed-clonefile.2:45-204,215-227",
        "installed-cp.1:136-145"
      ],
      "conclusion": "Regular-file fclonefileat from read-only source fd into an owned parent fd uses exact int,int,char*,uint32 ABI and flags3; no cp/copy fallback. Distinct inode/nlink and streaming source-vs-clone SHA checks, metadata pins, same-filesystem check and final source inventory prevent a falsely accepted changed source or shared hard link. Max256entries/depth16/logical6GiB, 1MiB hashing blocks and >=8GiB free preflight bound memory/disk risk; CoW can still fail later with ENOSPC."
    },
    {
      "area": "Failure/cancellation and root ownership",
      "references": [
        "owned_sdk_image.py:104-168",
        "owned_arm64_smoke.py:43-47,102-162,215-267,297-455"
      ],
      "conclusion": "Adapter performs no subprocess/deletion/global SDK write; failures leave partial owned outputs for the caller. It re-attests ownership and calls cancellation checkpoints perentry and perhashblock. Real runner signal handler sets a flag rather than interrupting Popen registration; outer finally stops registered workers then removes only its attested root if cleanup has no errors. Integration must use a checkpoint that raises on this exact cancellation flag and must remain inside existing try/finally. No helper exception may be swallowed into a green result."
    },
    {
      "area": "CLI and AVD emulator routing",
      "references": [
        "owned_sdk_image.py:171-210",
        "owned_arm64_smoke.py:322-379",
        "avd-manager-cli20-bytecode-01.txt:2119-2267,3486-3499,3543-3604"
      ],
      "conclusion": "Direct Java argv supplies one toolsdir rooted beneath owned/sdk; strips six JVM option/classpath injections, sets owned home/tmp/errorfile and SDK variables. Installed public classpath is read, not modified. Generated image.sysdir.1 must exactly match selected relativeimage and sysdir2 must be absent; unexpected output is rejected instead of rewritten. Caller should add explicit returned owned -sysdir while retaining absolute installed adb/emulator paths and existing ownership/transport guards."
    },
    {
      "area": "Pure tests",
      "references": [
        "test_owned_sdk_image.py:1-216"
      ],
      "conclusion": "Fourteen distinct source-declared tests cover equal source/clone bytes + distinct inodes, isolated scanner-like writes, unsupported-clone propagation/no fallback, existing target preservation, bad links/specials/bounds, missing/drifted metadata, bad clone, source mutation, first-checkpoint cancellation/ownerloss, lowdisk, exact native ABI, argv/env and malformed config. FakeOwned and small fake_clone are intentionally test-only. They do not exercise actual APFS, CLI, emulator or finalizer after a midhash cancellation."
    }
  ],
